P0131 Mutating a heap root through peek_mut leaves its priority stale. src/binary_heap.rs:627. PeekMutInner::deref_mut returns the root without marking its sift flag, so dropping a guard after changing the value skips heap repair. With a Max heap built from [9,7,8,1], assigning 0 through peek_mut and letting the guard leave scope leaves peek() returning 0 rather than 8. Subsequent removals therefore violate the heap's priority ordering after an ordinary public-API mutation.

